                <pb facs="1472" n="1458" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg1458"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 LCC/13: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-01-28T23:00:00-04:00">January 28,
                            1944—11 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>711. Embassy’s 729, January 27, 8 p.m. Department’s idea is that at this stage
                    the enlarged Committee will evolve over-all propaganda policy plans. These plans
                    will remain in effect, if approved by higher authority, until changed by the
                    Committee. They will govern the preparation of the weekly directives and be
                    binding upon the OWI, PWE and appropriate Russian agencies unless or until
                    modified.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
